  "note": "Triennial election of the Dromore Urban Council, polled Wednesday 18 May 1949. There was no election; nominations were received for all nine seats and the nine were returned unopposed (Banbridge Chronicle, 7 May 1949, p. 3). Mr. Samuel Tinsley did not seek re-election; Mr. Gibson and Captain Johnston were additions to the old Council. Returned unopposed."
